     "tests_daily_summary": "that the operator will UNDERSTAND the summary — it proves the three questions are answered and that the day-boundary residual refuses rather than computes, not that the explanations land. Four blind spots: (a) most checks are substring assertions over the rendered text, so rewording a line silently breaks the guarantee while the tool still runs; (b) it verifies the numbers are PRESENT, never that they are RIGHT — a wrong wallet balance formatted correctly passes every check here; (c) the external-flow line says money is 'probably in spot' when TRANSFER is zero, which is an inference we cannot verify because the system has no spot-wallet access at all; (d) it runs on whatever the ledger currently holds, so a day with no rotation exercises none of the Q2 path and still goes green Its Q2/day-boundary prose checks are conditional on the nav-row count the tool itself reports for its `--since` window (round 5, 2026-09-10): on a state copy older than 24h they print NOT EXERCISED rather than pass or fail — so a green run on a stale copy proves nothing about those two lines. W2 2026-09-12: `account_facts` now reports realised P&L as a RECORD (USDT-only slice; non-USDT amounts listed UNCONVERTED, never summed; `realised_pnl=None` ⇒ not observable and the same-day residual refuses; a truncated income read is labelled incomplete; a pre-split row is passed through under a STATED assumption) and the per-anchor cost column uses the three buckets — both asserted on fields with the reviewer's two counterexamples as inline mutations and on real ledger rows; it still cannot CONVERT a foreign-asset fee, only name it. Round 3 (2026-09-13, researcher REVIEW §3.C): the same-day residual's flow term is now the INTERVAL difference of the day-cumulative `external_flow_usdt` (the old form subtracted a day total from an interval equity change and read -1000 on a window where nothing happened) and refuses when either endpoint is not a finite number. Two further blind spots it does NOT close: (e) the interval form is exact only because the residual is computed same-day, where both endpoints share one 00:00Z origin — nothing here re-derives that the carrier really is cumulative, it is read from `binance_broker.income_since`; (f) a zero residual is not proof the account identity holds — it means the three terms we CAN read cancel, and any movement none of them carries (a fee type outside `realised_components`, a spot transfer) is invisible to it. Round 4 (2026-09-13, researcher round-3 monitoring NAV-R3-1): the equity endpoints (start and end nav, end wallet and unrealised) and each day's closing flow are read with the same three states as realised income — a finite 0 is a value, None / NaN / inf are not observable, and an endpoint is never replaced by 0 or by the other endpoint — so a start equity of 0 no longer turns into the end equity (-100 printed on a deposit into an empty account) and a NaN equity no longer marks the residual computable; an unknown maker intent refuses the fill-rate instead of shrinking its denominator. Pre-fix readers fail 29 of its round-4 cells. Two further blind spots: (g) these are CAPABILITY cells — the ledger copy (251 nav rows, 74,860 order rows) holds no None, NaN or zero equity, so they run on synthetic rows and two temp-ledger runs of main, never on a real day where it happened; (h) FIXED by E7 (FX-EXEC 2026-09-13): a window with no nav row renders the account as NOT OBSERVABLE and names the ledger's newest row as before the window and not used ([E7-a], the entry point on a temp ledger); the four [B3] account-text promises that were exercised only through the stale-row fallback (Q1, Q3, the sight boundary, the rotation line) are now NOT EXERCISED on a window without a nav row, like Q2, and E7-a4 asserts the NOT OBSERVABLE account in that case.",
